From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 11:10:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] UefiPayloadPkg: An 11 MiB FD for a release build, 12 MiB for
 a debug one

The firmware device of the payload, its image in memory, is 10 MiB in a
release build and 11 in a debug one. With Secure Boot, the LVGL setup,
the capsule update, iPXE and CSMWrap the DXE volume of a release build
is past 10 MiB and GenFv stops: "the required fv image size 0xa6b520
exceeds the set fv image size 0xa00000". With the firmware update
screen as well (UpdateScreenLib), the payload volume of a debug build,
iPXE and CSMWrap left out, no longer fits in 11 MiB. 11 MiB for a
release build and 12 for a debug one: it is memory the payload takes
while it runs, not flash, which holds the compressed image.

Co-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018n3yuWwDLW63F4vdf7ZFTv
---
 UefiPayloadPkg/UefiPayloadPkg.fdf | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/UefiPayloadPkg/UefiPayloadPkg.fdf b/UefiPayloadPkg/UefiPayloadPkg.fdf
index 4353556..76e1db1 100644
--- a/UefiPayloadPkg/UefiPayloadPkg.fdf
+++ b/UefiPayloadPkg/UefiPayloadPkg.fdf
@@ -18,11 +18,11 @@ DEFINE FD_SIZE     = 0x00850000
 DEFINE NUM_BLOCKS  = 0x850
 !else
 !if $(TARGET) == DEBUG
-DEFINE FD_SIZE     = 0x0B00000
-DEFINE NUM_BLOCKS  = 0xB00
+DEFINE FD_SIZE     = 0x0C00000
+DEFINE NUM_BLOCKS  = 0xC00
 !else
-DEFINE FD_SIZE     = 0x0A00000
-DEFINE NUM_BLOCKS  = 0xA00
+DEFINE FD_SIZE     = 0x0B00000
+DEFINE NUM_BLOCKS  = 0xB00
 !endif
 !endif
 
